Subject: [PATCH] Papo: furnace zero-listener gates for
 FurnaceBurn/StartSmelt/Smelt events
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Every fuel consume, every smelt start and every produced item built CraftItemStack
mirrors, CraftBlock wrappers, toBukkitRecipe() conversions and event objects even
with no plugin listening. Gate all three on their listener tables:

- FurnaceBurnEvent: own HandlerList, no subclasses, constructor stores burnTime
  raw (clamp lives in setBurnTime), burning/consumeFuel default true — with zero
  listeners callEvent() is always true and every getter returns its default, so
  the default flow is reproduced statement-for-statement.
- FurnaceStartSmeltEvent: declares no HandlerList; its listeners register into
  InventoryBlockStartEvent's table (shared with BrewingStartEvent/
  CampfireStartEvent), so an empty table provably means nobody can observe it.
  Not Cancellable; getTotalCookTime() defaults to the constructor arg.
- FurnaceSmeltEvent: declares no HandlerList; it is BlockCookEvent's only
  subclass so BlockCookEvent's table is authoritative. Round-trip lemma
  (CraftItemStack.java:106-113,133-138,439-454): asBukkitCopy(x) =
  asCraftMirror(x.copy()), asNMSCopy(craft) = craft.handle.copy(), and
  CraftItemStack.isSimilar == ItemStack.isSameItemSameComponents when both
  handles are non-null — with zero listeners the event round-trip yields a
  content-identical fresh copy (here the exclusive assemble() output itself)
  and the isSimilar check is exactly the NMS comparison.

